lity instead to prolong her utility on the field.","acc":[{"label":"Best","main":"Guts","main_info":{"icon":"L-Guts.webp","key":"Guts","tier":"L","label":"Guts","value":"150% ATK Barrier, 4 turns"},"sub":"DOT","sub_info":{"icon":"UC-DOT.webp","key":"DOT","tier":"UC","label":"Any DOT","value":""}},{"label":"Alt 1","main":"Bleed","main_info":{"icon":"UC-Bleed.webp","key":"Bleed","tier":"UC","label":"Bleed","value":"15% chance"},"sub":"Burn","sub_info":{"icon":"UC-Burn.webp","key":"Burn","tier":"UC","label":"Burn","value":"15% chance"}},{"label":"Alt 2","main":"Burn","main_info":{"icon":"UC-Burn.webp","key":"Burn","tier":"UC","label":"Burn","value":"15% chance"},"sub":"Poison","sub_info":{"icon":"UC-Poison.webp","key":"Poison","tier":"UC","label":"Poison","value":"15% chance"}},{"label":"Alt 3","main":"Poison","main_info":{"icon":"UC-Poison.webp","key":"Poison","tier":"UC","label":"Poison","value":"15% chance"},"sub":"Bleed","sub_info":{"icon":"UC-Bleed.webp","key":"Bleed","tier":"UC","label":"Bleed","value":"15% chance"}}]}],"dedicated":{"name":"Ariel's Starry Magic Book","main_stat":"MATK +247","icon":"Ariel.webp","a":[{"name":"Resilience","value":"+15%","icon":"Resilience.webp"},{"name":"Resilience","value":"+15%","icon":"Resilience.webp"},{"name":"Resilience","value":"+15%","icon":"Resilience.webp"},{"name":"Resilience","value":"+15%","icon":"Resilience.webp"}],"b":[{"name":"EffectHit","value":"+10%","icon":"EffectHit.webp"},{"name":"EffectHit","value":"+10%","icon":"EffectHit.webp"},{"name":"EffectHit","value":"+10%","icon":"EffectHit.webp"},{"name":"EffectHit","value":"+10%","icon":"EffectHit.webp"}],"second":"no","why_by_stat":{"Resilience":"Reduces incoming Critical Damage 1%-for-1%, helping Ariel survive Critical Hits more easily."},"story":"\"The most fundamental and basic movements are what constitute the most powerful strikes. If you build upon them, one by one, then any attack you launch can become the ultimate assault.\"\n\nAs a child who aspired to become a mage, Ariel received the \"Starry Magic Book\" as a gift from her older brother. She dismissed it as too basic at first, but later —troubled by her inability to control her vast magical powers— she remembered her brother's advice and returned to the book once more. Realizing the vital importance of the fundamentals, Ariel mastered the magic of starlight, always keeping the book close as a reminder of that lesson."},"used_in":[{"tip":"Power Up Dungeon: Earth","cat":"pve","banner":"PU_DUNGEON_EARTH.webp"},{"tip":"Castle Rush: Rachel","cat":"pve","banner":"CR_RACHEL.webp"},{"tip":"Castle Rush: Jave","cat":"pve","banner":"CR_JAVE.webp"},{"tip":"Advent Expedition: Yeonhee","cat":"pve","banner":"ADVENT_YH.webp"},{"tip":"Power Up Dungeon: Gold","cat":"pve","banner":"PU_DUNGEON_GOLD.webp"}],"lore":"Ariel is a polite and kind rabbit beastkin.\nShe is a war orphan, much like Rudy, and looks up to him since they grew up in the same orphanage.\nShe began to study light magic after seeing him use the power of light. Her spells have names like Light's Judgment, Dazzling Light, and Blessing of God.\nShe's often praised by the townspeople as being very polite and kind, but she also has a stubborn side to her.\nShe doesn't like Kris, who is competing against Rudy for the title of Knight of Light, and she also doesn't like all the women who've taken an interest in her childhood friend.\nShe likes all things cute, so she enjoys Snipper's company. She also thinks that Evan is pretty admirable for all of the things she's heard about him from Rudy.\nAfter graduating from the Magic Academy, she joins the Evan Expedition at Rudy's request."}